-- deliverable_category_selected
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='c) category of deliverable as an output of the validation/verification process, such as an issued assurance opinion or report; | The categories of deliverables (outputs) provided to the client after validation/verification of declared sustainability information using the ISO 14019 series include: a) assurance statements and opinions; b) non-assurance deliverables. NOTE 1 Issued deliverables can be used as stand-alone outputs by clients as well as by other conformity assessment bodies using it as input to their activities. NOTE 2 Examples of non-assurance deliverables include AUP reports, evidence reports and findings reports. — printed pp.16, 20 (PDF pp.22, 26)', verification_note='VA-verified 2026-09-08 (§7.5 c) and §6.1.1, printed pp.16, 20 (PDF pp.22, 26) — the printed top-level split is two-valued (assurance / non-assurance); the three non-assurance members are printed as EXAMPLES ("Examples of non-assurance deliverables include"), so the 4-value enum closes an examples list (see the STAGED file)) [VA · ISO 14019-1:2026 published First edition 2026-02, PDF text layer]', verified_at=now() where id='e2ce8caf-3ef6-4106-86c8-6f065210c126' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- team_competence_criteria
